        <headline>Hurricane Watch issued September 23 at 4:56PM HST by NWS Honolulu HI</headline>
        <description>* WHAT...East winds 25 to 35 kt with higher gusts and seas 13 to
18 feet.

* WHERE...Big Island Windward Waters.

* WHEN...Beginning 6 AM HST Friday.

* IMPACTS...Extremely strong winds will cause hazardous seas
which will likely capsize or damage vessels and severely
reduce visibility.
</description>
        <instruction>Mariners should remain in port, alter course, and/or secure the
vessel for extreme conditions before conditions deteriorate
further.</instruction>
